
# Project Brief — ML Image Classification Containerization

## Project Overview

The project focuses on preparing a pretrained image classification model from `torchvision.models` for deployment using Docker.

Two container images will be created and compared: a baseline (fat) image and an optimized (slim) image.

## Business Goal

Ensure that the ML model can be deployed consistently, tested reliably, and maintained efficiently.

## Scope

- Package the same model and inference code into two Docker images.
- Validate that both images produce matching top-3 predictions.
- Compare image size and build performance.
- Assess readiness for local deployment using Docker Compose.
- Identify deployment risks and communicate results to stakeholders.

## Technical Requirements

- Fat image: `ml-infer-fat:1.0`, based on `python:3.13`.
- Slim image: `ml-infer-slim:1.0`, based on `python:3.13-slim`, using a multi-stage build.
- Shared model artifact: `model/model.pt`.
- Shared inference script: `app/inference.py`.

## Expected Deliverables

- Technical task for the AI/ML team.
- Acceptance criteria.
- Docker image review checklist.
- Optimization comparison report.
- Docker Compose readiness checklist.
- Risk register.
- Stakeholder summary.

## Success Criteria

Both images must build and run successfully, produce matching inference results for the same test input, and provide measurable evidence for comparing deployment efficiency.

## Current Status

Planning and documentation phase. Implementation and testing results have not yet been verified.
